DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("sin(((ln(x))^2-4*(sin(x))+1))");
$fun_1 = Formula("((x^4)^5)^5");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("({1, 6} - {1, 6})");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("[8, infinity) U {1, 6} U {1, 6}");
$set_ans_6 = Compute("{1, 6} U {1, 6} U [8, infinity)");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("([1, 5]) U [1, infinity)");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("[1, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - [1, 5]) U [1, infinity) U [1, infinity) - ((-infinity, infinity) - [1, infinity))");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("[1, infinity) U [1, infinity) U [1, infinity) U [1, 5] - ((-infinity, infinity) - [1, 5])");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

What is the value of [`13+8/1`]? [_____]{answer=>21,width=>8}
---

[`0+19-8-15`] is equal to [_____]{Real(-4.)}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | 1 \leq x \leq 5\}`]
- [`B = \{x | x \geq 1\}`]

Compute:
- [`(A) \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`B \cap A \cup B \cup B \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`B \cup B \cup B \cup A \cap A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{x | x \geq 8\}`]
- [`B = \{1, 6\}`]

Compute:
- [`B - B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`A \cup B \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}
- [`B \cup B \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_6}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 10, -1, 7 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle 7, -8, 6 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 8, 2, -7 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<7, -8, 6>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<10, -1, 7>"))}
- [` \vec{w} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<8, 2, -7>") . Compute("<10, -1, 7>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<10, -1, 7>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<8, 2, -7>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle -2, -9, -6 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -10, 8, -7 \rangle `]

Compute:
- [` \vec{u} \times \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-2, -9, -6>") x Compute("<-10, 8, -7>")}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<-2, -9, -6>"))}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-10, 8, -7>") . Compute("<-2, -9, -6>")}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{v} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-2, -9, -6>") . Compute("<-10, 8, -7>")}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f'(7) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>7)}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>2)}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
